    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-003",
      "title": "Regular -er verbs in the present",
      "explanation": "Most French verbs end in -er, like parler (to speak). Drop -er and add the ending for the subject: je parle, tu parles, il/elle/on parle, nous parlons, vous parlez, ils/elles parlent. The -e, -es and -ent forms sound the same. To ask a yes/no question, put est-ce que before the statement (Est-ce que tu parles anglais ?) or simply raise your voice at the end (Tu parles anglais ?).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Nous parlons français.",
          "en": "We speak French."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Ils regardent un film.",
          "en": "They are watching a film."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Est-ce que tu travailles demain ?",
          "en": "Are you working tomorrow?"
        }
      ],
